    "physical_investigation": {
      "factor_1_henderson_hasselbalch_pk": "Rehman Fig. 7 cites pK = 6.75 with delta_A = 3.290 and delta_B = 5.805 ppm. In physiological literature (Moon 1973, Dawson 1977), pK at 37 C and physiological ionic strength ranges from 6.75 to 6.80. A pK shift of +0.05..+0.06 accounts for the discrepancy.",
      "factor_2_jmrui_chemical_shift_referencing": "In jMRUI AMARES peak fitting, PCr is typically referenced to 0.00 ppm rather than -2.54 ppm. If delta_o in the authors' analysis script was computed from unrounded jMRUI chemical shifts with an internal zero reference, a ~0.08 ppm difference in peak assignment shifts calculated pH by ~0.06.",
      "factor_3_spreadsheet_rounding": "The published Dryad spreadsheet rounds chemical shifts to 2 decimal places (-2.54, 2.26, 2.31). Sub-ppm precision in original FID spectra fitting is lost during Excel export.",
      "epistemic_ruling": "Per scientific integrity guidelines, NO artificial empirical correction factor (+0.055) is added to the code. Status PH_CALIBRATION_PARTIAL is retained. Neither pure aerobic metabolism nor complete absence of proton accumulation can be claimed solely from relative PCr and Pi peaks without independent blood lactate and acid-base measurements."
